   * Products with visibility set to 'deleted' or 'suspended' return a 404 response. Products with visibility 'unavailable_but_visible' (no variants) return successfully with variant data empty but the product details still shown as unavailable for purchase.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param productId Unique identifier (UUID) of the product to retrieve. Must reference an existing product whose visibility is not 'deleted' or 'suspended'.
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor customer
   * @x-autobe-specification Query e_commerce_mall_products by id with UUID equality filter. If product does not exist or visibility is 'deleted' or 'suspended', return 404 Not Found. Join e_commerce_mall_seller_profiles to retrieve shop_name. Left join e_commerce_mall_categories to retrieve category name and description (nullable if category was deleted). Include e_commerce_mall_product_images where deleted_at IS NULL, ordered by sort_order ascending — the first image (lowest sort_order) is the thumbnail. Include e_commerce_mall_product_variants where deleted_at IS NULL, ordered by created_at ascending. For each variant, include e_commerce_mall_product_variant_options where deleted_at IS NULL (key-value option pairs). For each variant, calculate current stock by summing quantity_change from all e_commerce_mall_inventory_records for that variant. If visibility is 'unavailable_but_visible' (no variants exist), mark purchasable flag as false. Include e_commerce_mall_reviews where deleted_at IS NULL, ordered by created_at DESC. For each review, join e_commerce_mall_customer_profiles to get the customer's display name (if customer deleted their account, use 'deleted user'). Calculate average rating by averaging rating from all non-deleted reviews. Calculate total review count by counting non-deleted reviews.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Get(":productId")
  public async at(
    @CustomerAuth()
    customer: CustomerPayload,
    @TypedParam("productId")
    productId: string & tags.Format<"uuid">,
  ): Promise<IECommerceMallProduct> {
    try {
      return await getECommerceMallCustomerProductsProductId({
        customer,
        productId,
      });
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(error);
      throw error;
    }
  }
